@voice navarro-mateo
// Works writer. Mateo Navarro (he/him): Works systems officer, night shift, cabin 4-15. Reliable, sharp-eyed. Runs
// the board overnight; keeps one of the ship's four lost-property boxes (each keeper thinks they're the only one).
// A twin on the Halcyon (one of the Halcyon's three Wren twins). Gym regular, runner; up by early afternoon.
//
// HOW HE TALKS: calm, exact, unhurried. Short sentences, no fuss. Says "It'll turn up" about almost anything, and
// it usually does. Mentions small things kindly ("Your collar's folded. There.").
// WITH JUNIORS: patient; shows rather than tells; never makes you feel slow. Leaves the day team neat handover
// notes with headings.
// WHAT HE NOTICES: what's out of place, and whose it is. A spanner on the wrong hook. A missing glove.
// MOOD TELLS: low = reorganises the lost-property box; high = hums while he tidies the board.
// NEVER: hurries; gossips about whose things turn up where; talks about his twin before friend tier.
// RUNNING: the lost-property box ("Third glove this week. Same hand."); the other three boxes he hasn't heard of;
// the handover notes, with a summary at the top.
tpl: steady
talk: Calm, exact, unhurried; short sentences; notices small things and mentions them kindly; "It'll turn up."
cares: the board tidy for the day shift | the lost-property box | handover notes done properly | his twin on the Halcyon
jokes: everything lost on the Wren ends up in his box, and he knows whose it is | there are three other boxes he doesn't know about | his handover notes have headings and a summary
hi: Hello | Evening | There you are
bye: Mind how you go | Take care, then | See you at handover
yes: Can do | Noted | Leave it with me
thanks: Thank you | Much obliged | That's a help
wow: Well, now | That's neat work
sigh: Ah well | It'll turn up
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: listen
openness: normal
loves: book | tea
likes: card | game
invites: running | observatory
joy: the lost-property box, and putting things back in the right hands
thread: lonely
keepsake: a single odd glove from the box, "for when its twin turns up"
avoid: his twin, until friend tier | whose things he's found
